rg/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Ugland_House.jpg/960px-Ugland_House.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Mission sui iuris of the Cayman Islands","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":19.2767,"lo":-81.3868,"d":2073,"ds":"The Mission sui iuris of the Cayman Islands (Latin: Missio sui iuris Insularum Caimanensium) is a mission sui iuris of the Latin Church of the Catholic Church in the Caribbean. The mission comprises the entirety of the British dependency of the Cayman Islands and consists of five parishes, including Saint Ignatius in George Town, Christ the Redeemer Church in West Bay, and Stella Maris Church on Cayman Brac.","wpu":"Mission sui iuris of the Cayman Islands","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/20/Cayman_Islands-CIA_WFB_Map.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},{"n":"Watler Cemetery","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":19.274,"lo":-81.335,"d":5552,"ds":"The Watler Cemetery is a historic cemetery located in Prospect, Grand Cayman. It was donated to the National Trust for the Cayman Islands by the Watler family in 1991. Although the graves in the cemetery date from the beginning of the 19th century, the site was in use before that time, as Watlers have lived in the Cayman Islands since the 17th century and are among the original settlers of Cayman.","wpu":"Watler Cemetery","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/e/e8/Watler_Cemetery_Grand_Cayman.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},{"n":"Hell, Grand Cayman","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":19.37935,"lo":-81.40678,"d":9705,"ds":"Hell is an area within the district of West Bay, Grand Cayman. Its name comes from a group of short, black, limestone formations located in the area. Its eerie and rather sinister look is what gave it its infamous name.","wpu":"Hell, Grand Cayman","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/Hell_Grand_Cayman_%281%29.JPG/960px-Hell_Grand_Cayman_%281%29.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"}],"about":{"ds":"Grand Cayman is the largest of the three Cayman Islands and the location of the territory's capital, George Town. In relation to the other two Cayman Islands, it is approximately 75 miles (121 km) southwest of Little Cayman and 90 miles (145 km) southwest of Cayman Brac.","wpu":"Grand Cayman","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Grand_cayman.jpg/960px-Grand_cayman.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},"wk":"2026-10-18"}